elieve that the benevolent  deku tree would ask to talk to link  personally and not mido and of course  there's also a girl involved saria you  know the sage of the forest who mido  clearly had feelings for yet was never  able to get serious to notice him like  she did link and there's also the fact  that the deku tree dies after link goes  to see him so yeah i can understand why  he'd be a bit salty of course it still  doesn't make it right anyway that was  mido most ocarina of time players  remember him as some jerk and move on  but later on in the game after link  obtains all three spiritual stones as a  kid and opens the door of time in the  temple of time and claims the master  sword for his own and subsequently  allows ganondorf free access to the  triforce  as most know link is then able to travel  into the future by seven years and  explore the shattered world of hyrule as  an adult if you go back to the kokori  forest which you do have to do in order  to complete the forest temple you'll  notice that monsters abound where they  previously did not talk to a cokery  child inside of serious house and  they'll tell you that mido said that the  great deku tree withered because a boy  named link did something wrong to it and  only seria defended link before she left  to the forest temple talk to another  kokri in mido's house and they'll tell  you that the monsters are here because  of the deku tree's death now this is  some pretty pertinent information  because it's made clear to us that not  only was the deku tree's death pinned on  link by mido but that also means that  since monsters are now ruining the once  peaceful kokori forest due to maido  spreading this misinformation about link  killing the deku tree the kokori now  associate link with the appearance of  the monsters and therefore now hate link  all of them do except for seria  according to that cokery in series house  fast forward a bit and link has to  traverse the lost woods in order to find  the forest temple and blocking the right  path once again is everyone's favorite  fiery redheaded shorty mido he doesn't  recognize you as link even though he  notices that you're wearing quote  co-curish clothing and refuses once  again to allow you passage until you  play serious song of course he notes  that seria only ever taught that song to  her close friends and though he's  confused as to who you are in light of  this he finally lets you pass so that  you can go and meet seria and complete  the forest temple after completing the  temple if you go back and talk to mido  link explains that seria isn't coming  back because she's now a sage to which  maida responds by saying his last and  most important lines in the entire game  oh i see serio won't ever come back but  i i made a promise to seria if link came  back i would be sure to tell him that  sarah had been waiting for him because  seria really  liked  hey you if you see him somewhere please  let him know and also i'm sorry for  being mean to him tell him that too and  after this you never speak to him again  though he is seen once more at the very  end of the game about halfway through  the credits roll the music and visuals  change pretty drastically into a full-on  outdoor dance party at lawn lawn ranch  involving pretty much everyone you meet  in the entire game and i do mean  everyone there's the gerudo the zora the  dancing couple even big goron and the  cokery children the dance party takes  place after link and zelda defeat  ganondorf at the end of the adult  timeline as evidenced by malin's age  since she's grown up by the time of this  dance party and it's assumed that  everyone is so happy and dancing and  having a good time because zelda after  the ending fight was able to retake her  kingdom as its rightful ruler and  explain to everyone the tale of link the  hero who traveled through time to defeat  the aforementioned ganondorf which is  why the tale of the hero of time has  become legend by the time the wind waker  takes place and since ganondorf is no  more that means they can all go back to  living their happy normal lives after  seven long years of serving an evil king  it's a happy time which is why there's  something so off about one of the  characters who appears here see the  cokery are dancing and playing around  and having a good time but one of them  is not you don't see mida with the other  children in fact you don't see him at  all until after the music dies down and  he's shown to be sitting away from  everyone else alone well not alone he's  got the zora king with him but i'm sure  the zora king is just sitting out there  because he can't very well do much else  now can he and moving anywhere would  probably take him about  the essence of the sages causes mido to  briefly look skyward but then the camera  zooms off and that's it for the scene  and mido it always struck me as  strangely important that mida would be  secluding himself from everyone else  looking sadly at the ground why would he  be over here sulking it up when there's  a party to be had involving everyone  including all his close friends in the  cokery being sad because of losing seria  is one thing but most of the people  dancing around the fire have also lost a  notable member of their people groups  due to the calling of the sages yet  there's still plenty of cause for  celebration i.e the defeat of ganondorf  i think mido's sulking behavior here was  meant to tell us a story about how he's  responding to the news about link saving  the world and let me explain that  further by way of a question what is the  only difference between mido and  everyone else at the party the  difference is maida was the only person  in the entire world of hyrule who didn't  believe in link not only that he's the  only person who actually tried to stop  link and put him down being jealous of  him the entire time and we know that  these kinds of self-aware sorrowful  emotions were somewhere inside him  because of his words to adult link where  he says that he's sorry for how he  treated link as a child he said that to  a complete stranger adult meaning he's  dealing with immense feelings of guilt  now i could end the episode right here  and say that prideful kid gets sad out  of guilt and that's the end of the story  and if you only looked at ocarina of  time that's really all you could get  from this information but there's one  more mention of mido later on in the  zelda series that got my theory senses  tingling see if you fast forward all the  way to the end of the fallen timeline  which is the alternate adult timeline  that takes place if link is killed by  ganondorf instead of killing ganondorf  enabling ganondorf to take the triforce  4 himself you eventually come to the  last game in the timeline zelda 2 the  adventure of link in the game there are  seven notable towns eight if you include  the ruins of old kasuto some of the  towns are named after the sages from  ocarina of time the towns of syria  darunia ruto rauru and naburu now in  real life of course since zelda 2 came  out a good decade before ocarina of time  clearly the town names were the  inspirations for the names of the sages  as far as development is concerned but  in regards to in-universe lore since  ocarina of time takes place before zelda  2 the towns were in turn actually named  after the sages which makes sense since  the hero of time would have fallen in  this timeline according to the backstory  of a link to the past the sages and  people of hyrule were the ones who  stepped up to seal ganondorf within the  sacred realm no doubt exalting their  statuses as heroes which is definitely  worth naming a town after but there are  a few town names i didn't mention the  final three are named kasito old kasuto  and the harbour town of maido that's  right maido has a town named after him  in the fallen timeline now names in  zelda games are always extremely  important i mean half of zelda theories  out there are based off of similar names  and for good reason kakariko is always  called kakariko beetle is always called  beel and imba is always called impa  right the zelda dev team have always  used names to connect pieces of lore or  locations over the metanarrative that is  the universe of zelda so that begs the  question if the towns of zelda 2 are  mostly named after the sages who are the  heroes of the people what could mido  have possibly done to exalt his status  in a similar manner you could say it's  because he was the leader of the kokori  but seria is already a sage of the  cokery which pretty much overshadows  anything mido could have been by just  being their boss i think it's something  different so let's rewind once again to  the party scene at the end of ocarina of  time notice that the kokori are outside  of the kokori forest which is something  that the kokari said earlier in the game  would kill them if they left according  to the deku tree clearly though they're  not dead so what does this actually mean  the deku tree wouldn't lie right in my  opinion since link and the kokori  children of the lost woods were based on  and heavily inspired by peter pan and  the eternally child like lost boys which  miyamoto confirmed in an interview with  the french magazine game cult it  probably means that leaving the lost  woods would result in the cokery giving  up their immortal forms as children and  aging as a normal human being would of  course leaving neverland leading to  aging is debatable in peter pan lore but  the movie hook which featured an aged  peter pan for the first time played by  the actor and zelda fanatic robin  williams may he rest in peace did come  out in 1991 a full seven years before  ocarina of time so the very famous movie  could have inspired the idea we do also  have some slight in-universe evidence of  this being true though what i'm about to  say could easily be an entire theory  video on its own but let's jump over to  the child timeline which takes place  before ganondorf is able to conquer  hyrule but yet does not feature the deku  tree the cokery or their evolved forms  the koroks or does it see it's been a  theory for a while now that the people  of oron village may actually be the  kokori that turned mortal and aged a bit  due to several reasons which i'll state  briefly one they border the fair on  woods which has the forest temple inside  it which is a get this giant  hollowed-out tree with a parasite living  inside that you have to cleanse with the  cocaine symbol literally all over the  inside sound familiar add this to the  fact that a blond-haired ordonian man is  named fedo and in the alternate adult  timeline there is a blonde-haired  cockery named fedo could twilight  princesses fado and ordonian villagers  be the cokery who left the forest or  protection of the deku tree and  therefore began to age as mortals like i  said it's a theory in and of itself but  for the purposes of this video let's  just assume for a moment that it is true  now back to the theory in the downfall  timeline this party would not have taken  place instead people would learn that  ganondorf had killed link the hero which  is kind of a bummer this means that it  was up to the sages and the people of  hyrule to fight against ganon's forces  that would soon be pouring out of the  dark world this event is called the  imprisoning war in zelda lore and it is  the only thing that we know of that  happens between ocarina of time and a  link to the past and notably the rest of  the timeline following a link to the  past features no cokery or deku tree so  something tells me that whatever mido  did to make a name for himself to the  hylians who would have been the ones to  name the towns of zelda 2 it would have  had to happen after ocarina of time and  before a link to the past in the  imprisoning war so here's my speculation  based on everything we've talked about  could it be that mido the one who  assumedly already knows how to use a  sword and a shield and who was jealous  of link being called upon to be a hero  by the deku tree heard about link  falling heroically in combat against  ganondorf who was also responsible for  killing the deku tree by the way and due  to his guilt and newfound sense of  vengeance decided to leave the kokori  forest to join the fight against ganon  potentially even taking the cokery with  him and what if this war lasted a while  like wars can years even which would  have been long enough for mido and  potentially the other kokori children to  grow up and what if this led to mido  becoming a war hero the leader of the  kokori army it is an intense contrast to  the kid bully that we grew up knowing  but given all the facts across the zelda  universe and the disappearance of the  kokiri following the events of ocarina  of time i think this is the best answer  to why maida would have his name exalted  to the status of the sages but of course  this is all just my theory there are  still things we don't know such as who  kasito is and why a town would be named  after them in that case and there is of  course the possibility that the name  mido was just that a name but what do  you guys think let me know in the  comments below also thank you so much  for watching please consider leaving a  like if you enjoyed the theory it helps  much more than you might know and  subscribe to stick around for all the  other juicy videos that i make about  your favorite games huge thanks as  always to my bandit crew who make these  videos possible including the fabulous  fellow youtuber hannah yosora who  recently joined the ranks of my elite if  you're interested in joining up please  feel free to check out the join button  below or in the description that's all  i've got for this one so as always i  hope you have a wonderful rest of your  day this is masterton abandoned looking  forward to seeing you next time and  signing out peace  [Music]  you

